1
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:20,530
I said I want to dream of sushi,

2
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:22,900
but with what you did,
it's like I'll have a nightmare.

3
00:00:22,901 --> 00:00:24,036
What's that?

4
00:00:24,036 --> 00:00:25,337
Paella negra.

5
00:00:25,337 --> 00:00:28,634
Even a stray dog who hasn't eaten for months
won't eat that.

6
00:00:28,634 --> 00:00:30,500
So you made a mango pie

7
00:00:30,501 --> 00:00:32,367
where mangoes were harvested
from just anywhere?

8
00:00:32,367 --> 00:00:34,069
That is not okay.

9
00:00:34,069 --> 00:00:37,633
I guess you're aware
that they are just playing with you.

10
00:00:37,634 --> 00:00:40,542
I can feel that they're challenging me.

11
00:00:40,542 --> 00:00:43,711
But don't worry,
tomorrow, I'll be okay again.

12
00:00:43,711 --> 00:00:45,080
I won't give up.

13
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:47,015
<i>Remember, you made a promise to me</i>

14
00:00:47,015 --> 00:00:48,817
that the moment you get tired there,

15
00:00:48,817 --> 00:00:50,852
you'll come home here as soon as possible.

16
00:00:50,852 --> 00:00:54,139
Can you still cook
for the naughty grandsons of Grandpa Garp?

17
00:00:54,139 --> 00:00:57,258
Or will you follow
what you promised to Mother and Father?

18
00:00:57,258 --> 00:01:00,095
Never ever give up, you can do it.

19
00:01:00,095 --> 00:01:02,530
Why are the Ferells like that
when it comes to food?

20
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:09,170
The late wife of Don Ferell, Dona Amanda,
is a very good cook.

21
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:11,573
When Dona Amanda died,

22
00:01:11,573 --> 00:01:14,342
it was like they don't care about each other.

23
00:01:14,342 --> 00:01:16,186
Do you know the saying,

24
00:01:16,186 --> 00:01:18,947
"the way to a man's heart
is through his stomach"?

25
00:01:18,947 --> 00:01:22,617
Your mother and I won't be a couple
if not for this recipe.

26
00:01:22,617 --> 00:01:24,366
Father, what are you cooking?

27
00:01:24,366 --> 00:01:28,645
This is what you call, "a heart that loves".

28
00:02:18,169 --> 00:02:20,640
So, who is my secret admirer?

29
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:24,677
In fairness, he's very sweet.

30
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:30,019
He sent messages using a dove.

31
00:02:30,019 --> 00:02:33,822
Whoever said that romance is dead?

32
00:02:33,822 --> 00:02:35,817
Your hair is long...

33
00:02:35,817 --> 00:02:37,662
Effort.

34
00:02:39,361 --> 00:02:44,700
He could give... chocolates or flowers,

35
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:48,370
but messages using a dove.

36
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:51,250
I even beat Harry Potter.

37
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:56,056
It's like I'm studying at Hogwart's
School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.

38
00:02:56,056 --> 00:03:00,360
I'm also happy I'll always taste
your loving heart.

39
00:03:03,152 --> 00:03:04,953
Is it Owen?

40
00:03:04,953 --> 00:03:07,156
Well...

41
00:03:07,156 --> 00:03:09,625
It seems you're in deep thought.

42
00:03:09,625 --> 00:03:12,528
You startled me.

43
00:03:12,528 --> 00:03:15,463
Do you know what's more startling?

44
00:03:35,517 --> 00:03:40,055
What, did you convince Don Ferell
to make his grandsons eat your food?

45
00:03:40,055 --> 00:03:42,157
Yes, Mr. Dencio.

46
00:03:42,157 --> 00:03:43,892
I told you.

47
00:03:43,892 --> 00:03:46,728
You can work as a cook here in the mansion.

48
00:03:46,728 --> 00:03:49,998
I wouldn't have thought about it
if not for you.

49
00:03:49,998 --> 00:03:54,565
You have a lot of insights about the Ferells,
that's why, thank you.

50
00:03:54,565 --> 00:03:56,972
What's with you? No problem.

51
00:03:56,972 --> 00:03:59,874
I'm already happy that I'm able to help you.

52
00:04:03,679 --> 00:04:07,249
Mr. Dencio, I have a question.

53
00:04:07,249 --> 00:04:11,987
Is there someone in the mansion
who's taking care of the doves?

54
00:04:11,987 --> 00:04:15,877
A dove?

55
00:04:16,992 --> 00:04:20,562
There's no one that I know
here in the mansion.

56
00:04:21,730 --> 00:04:23,866
Is there someone taking care
of the doves here?

57
00:04:23,866 --> 00:04:25,839
None.

58
00:04:25,839 --> 00:04:28,070
Do you have a pet dove?

59
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:31,431
None, but I have a lizard.

60
00:04:32,454 --> 00:04:34,076
Do you want a lizard?

61
00:04:34,076 --> 00:04:36,511
No, I don't want.

62
00:04:38,847 --> 00:04:44,086
How about our neighbors,
do they have pet doves?

63
00:04:44,086 --> 00:04:46,909
Neighbors?

64
00:04:46,909 --> 00:04:48,991
With how vast the property of Don Ferell is,

65
00:04:48,991 --> 00:04:52,261
I don't think we have neighbors here.

66
00:04:52,261 --> 00:04:56,638
Wait, why are you interested in doves?

67
00:04:56,638 --> 00:04:58,904
Not really.

68
00:05:00,736 --> 00:05:02,771
How about the Ferells?

69
00:05:02,771 --> 00:05:06,256
Do you know who among them is fond of doves?

70
00:05:07,287 --> 00:05:11,180
With doves, none.

71
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:15,517
It seems it's Owen who likes animals.

72
00:05:15,517 --> 00:05:17,619
Really?

73
00:05:17,619 --> 00:05:20,689
Yes, I remember.

74
00:05:20,689 --> 00:05:25,994
Owen wanted to get a puppy,
but it didn't push through,

75
00:05:25,994 --> 00:05:29,364
because Serafica is allergic.

76
00:05:29,364 --> 00:05:30,532
Yes, that's right.

77
00:05:30,532 --> 00:05:33,709
It's Owen who is the animal lover here.

78
00:05:37,139 --> 00:05:39,908
Hey, why are you smiling that way?

79
00:05:39,908 --> 00:05:41,810
It looks like you won the lottery.

80
00:05:41,810 --> 00:05:45,581
No, Mr. Dencio I'm just happy
when I meet someone

81
00:05:45,581 --> 00:05:47,482
who happens to be an animal lover like me.

82
00:05:47,482 --> 00:05:48,984
- Oh, is that so?
- Yes.

83
00:05:48,984 --> 00:05:51,286
You know, I'm an animal lover too.

84
00:05:51,286 --> 00:05:54,273
- I am fond of fish.
- Fish?

85
00:05:54,273 --> 00:05:56,358
Yes, fish.

86
00:05:56,358 --> 00:05:59,304
Then why are you eating fish?

87
00:05:59,304 --> 00:06:00,762
That's right.

88
00:06:00,762 --> 00:06:03,364
I'm a "fishtetarian".

89
00:06:08,570 --> 00:06:10,472
Go ahead and eat.

90
00:06:11,873 --> 00:06:13,875
Come on, Florence.

91
00:06:13,875 --> 00:06:15,610
Here, eat.

92
00:06:16,284 --> 00:06:17,713
It's delicious, right?

93
00:06:17,713 --> 00:06:22,083
- Fish be with you.
- Fish be with you?

94
00:06:34,696 --> 00:06:38,433
<i>I guess my hunch is right.</i>

95
00:06:38,433 --> 00:06:41,436
<i>No matter how proud and naughty
these guys are,</i>

96
00:06:41,436 --> 00:06:44,139
<i>they're all close to their grandfather.</i>

97
00:06:44,139 --> 00:06:48,043
<i>They just need a little push.</i>

98
00:06:48,043 --> 00:06:50,001
<i>Success!</i>

99
00:06:55,717 --> 00:07:01,990
<i>Are you just a dream, or will it come true?</i>

100
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:12,812
He's cute, and of all the Ferells,

101
00:07:12,812 --> 00:07:16,038
he's the only one I haven't heard talking.

102
00:07:16,038 --> 00:07:17,372
Why?

103
00:07:17,372 --> 00:07:19,207
Is he a weirdo?

104
00:07:19,207 --> 00:07:22,644
Or he sounds like a frog?

105
00:07:22,644 --> 00:07:25,814
Kokak, kokak, kokak.

106
00:07:26,448 --> 00:07:28,583
It's so delicious.

107
00:07:32,988 --> 00:07:35,665
Did he see me looking at him?

108
00:07:39,394 --> 00:07:41,032
Just kidding!

109
00:07:41,896 --> 00:07:43,571
There.

110
00:07:59,347 --> 00:08:02,907
My goodness...
Did he catch me looking at him?

111
00:08:02,907 --> 00:08:04,319
I hope not.

112
00:08:04,319 --> 00:08:06,822
He might think that I have a desire for him.

113
00:08:06,822 --> 00:08:09,658
Hello, I don't have a desire for him.

114
00:08:09,658 --> 00:08:13,587
Nothing, nothing, nothing!

115
00:08:13,587 --> 00:08:14,946
Stop it, Florencia.

116
00:08:14,946 --> 00:08:16,993
You're thinking a lot of nonsense, you witch.

117
00:08:16,993 --> 00:08:19,334
Well, you don't have a desire for Nero.

118
00:08:19,334 --> 00:08:22,001
Nothing, nothing, nothing!

119
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,743
Is there really nothing?

120
00:08:34,616 --> 00:08:36,218
Grandpa asked me to come here.

121
00:08:36,218 --> 00:08:37,719
He wants to talk to you.

122
00:08:37,719 --> 00:08:42,141
<i>So, this is the tone of his voice.</i>

123
00:08:42,141 --> 00:08:45,127
<i>He doesn't sound like a frog.</i>

124
00:08:45,127 --> 00:08:47,662
Did you hear what I said?

125
00:08:47,662 --> 00:08:48,830
Yes, frog.

126
00:08:48,830 --> 00:08:51,833
Yes, Grandpa Garp is asking for me.

127
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:54,068
I'll go to him right away.

128
00:08:59,341 --> 00:09:01,209
I want to thank you, Florence.

129
00:09:01,209 --> 00:09:04,775
Your idea that we eat together
with my grandsons

130
00:09:04,775 --> 00:09:07,849
is making this old man happy these days.

131
00:09:07,849 --> 00:09:13,099
Initially, I admit that I want to pinch
my grandsons' mouths

132
00:09:13,099 --> 00:09:18,427
because they were all frowning
when I said we will eat together.

133
00:09:18,427 --> 00:09:20,128
Good thing, these days,

134
00:09:20,128 --> 00:09:27,268
they're starting to be comfortable
eating together during meal time.

135
00:09:28,069 --> 00:09:30,906
That's what my mother taught me.

136
00:09:30,906 --> 00:09:35,844
Food doesn't become delicious
because of its delicious ingredients.

137
00:09:35,844 --> 00:09:40,482
It becomes more delicious
when you're eating it with your loved ones.

138
00:09:40,482 --> 00:09:42,452
Your parents are good people, Florence.

139
00:09:42,452 --> 00:09:44,252
They should be proud of you

140
00:09:44,252 --> 00:09:48,256
because it looks like
they've raised you well.

141
00:09:48,256 --> 00:09:51,999
Oh, don't give too much credit
to Mother and Father.

142
00:09:51,999 --> 00:09:57,098
I was born so beautiful and kind, perfect!

143
00:09:57,098 --> 00:10:00,134
See, Grandpa Garp, I'm a very ideal daughter.

144
00:10:01,436 --> 00:10:02,938
That's just a joke.

145
00:10:02,938 --> 00:10:06,074
And it's true that
Mother and Father are so kind,

146
00:10:06,074 --> 00:10:08,677
that's why, I owe it to them
whoever I am right now.

147
00:10:08,677 --> 00:10:11,179
So, I'll do everything for them

148
00:10:11,179 --> 00:10:15,057
and I won't replace them with anyone else.

149
00:10:15,057 --> 00:10:19,876
We are lucky that you became
a part of our family, Florence.

150
00:10:26,828 --> 00:10:29,841
Where are we going?

151
00:10:29,841 --> 00:10:33,568
I need to drop by GU
to talk to the Academic Dean

152
00:10:33,568 --> 00:10:36,438
to know the academic status of my grandsons.

153
00:10:36,438 --> 00:10:38,809
School is about to start.

154
00:10:45,213 --> 00:10:48,517
This is Gyronella University.

155
00:10:48,517 --> 00:10:52,420
The best university in the country.

156
00:11:06,171 --> 00:11:08,570
- Hi, Dean.
- Welcome, Don Ferell.

157
00:11:08,570 --> 00:11:09,704
Welcome.

158
00:11:09,704 --> 00:11:11,468
Florence?

159
00:11:13,642 --> 00:11:16,444
Florence, Don Ferell is calling you.

160
00:11:16,444 --> 00:11:17,650
I'm sorry.

161
00:11:17,650 --> 00:11:19,014
I got distracted.

162
00:11:19,014 --> 00:11:21,189
GU is really beautiful.

163
00:11:21,189 --> 00:11:22,417
Do you need anything?

164
00:11:22,417 --> 00:11:26,321
No, I just wanted to tell you
that you can stay in the car with Dencio.

165
00:11:26,321 --> 00:11:27,690
Okay. No problem.

166
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:29,658
We'll wait for you here.

167
00:11:30,458 --> 00:11:31,434
- Okay.
- Shall we?

168
00:11:31,434 --> 00:11:32,860
Shall we?

169
00:11:35,463 --> 00:11:36,998
Beautiful...

170
00:11:36,998 --> 00:11:39,267
It looks like a mall.

171
00:11:40,251 --> 00:11:43,605
Mr. Dencio, can I call my Mother and Father?

172
00:11:43,605 --> 00:11:44,839
- Okay, go ahead.
- I'll just stroll around.

173
00:11:44,839 --> 00:11:46,844
- Go ahead.
- I will be quick.

174
00:11:48,410 --> 00:11:49,678
Mother, Father?

175
00:11:49,678 --> 00:11:52,780
- Don't go too far.
- I'll be quick.

176
00:12:02,857 --> 00:12:04,540
Someone is calling.

177
00:12:05,427 --> 00:12:06,586
Hey, Florence.

178
00:12:06,586 --> 00:12:08,063
Why are you calling?

179
00:12:08,063 --> 00:12:09,931
- Is that Florence?
- Yes.

180
00:12:09,931 --> 00:12:11,933
My child!

181
00:12:11,933 --> 00:12:13,568
Is there a problem?

182
00:12:13,568 --> 00:12:16,805
Father, there's no problem,
but guess where I am right now?

183
00:12:16,805 --> 00:12:18,907
I hope you're still on earth, my child.

184
00:12:18,907 --> 00:12:22,944
Yes, I'll get mad if you went ahead of me.

185
00:12:22,944 --> 00:12:24,179
<i>What's with you?</i>

186
00:12:24,179 --> 00:12:27,882
I'm still here on earth,
but I'm in the coolest place.

187
00:12:30,290 --> 00:12:32,721
You're in the Gyronella University, Florence?

188
00:12:32,721 --> 00:12:34,126
Yes, Mother. Yes, Father!

189
00:12:34,126 --> 00:12:36,625
Welcome to Gyronella University.

190
00:12:36,625 --> 00:12:38,526
Welcome to GU.

191
00:12:38,526 --> 00:12:40,428
<i>Let's stroll around. Let's go!</i>

192
00:12:40,428 --> 00:12:42,565
Go ahead, my child.

193
00:12:42,565 --> 00:12:44,000
Let's start here...

194
00:12:46,901 --> 00:12:49,704
Mother, Father,
I think this is their soccer field.

195
00:12:49,704 --> 00:12:51,422
Look, it's so big.

196
00:12:51,422 --> 00:12:53,308
<i>Let's try it, Mother.</i>

197
00:12:53,308 --> 00:12:55,377
Excuse me, can I try?

198
00:12:55,377 --> 00:12:57,512
There you go, Mother...

199
00:12:57,512 --> 00:13:00,481
Here, Mother. One, two, three...

200
00:13:01,516 --> 00:13:04,919
Yes! Yes! Goal!

201
00:13:04,919 --> 00:13:07,055
Thank you!

202
00:13:07,055 --> 00:13:09,690
Someone is trying out
for the volleyball team here.

203
00:13:11,185 --> 00:13:13,518
Let me... Let me!

204
00:13:18,099 --> 00:13:20,101
Alyssa Valdez.

205
00:13:20,101 --> 00:13:22,151
<i>Thank you. Bye!</i>

206
00:13:22,151 --> 00:13:23,905
<i>Let's go here.</i>

207
00:13:23,905 --> 00:13:25,763
Mother, Father,
this is their basketball court.

208
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,264
Someone is playing.

209
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:30,678
There...

210
00:13:31,413 --> 00:13:33,248
There!

211
00:13:33,248 --> 00:13:34,749
There!

212
00:13:36,918 --> 00:13:37,952
I can do that better.

213
00:13:37,952 --> 00:13:39,921
Let me try, Mister...

214
00:13:39,921 --> 00:13:41,517
Can you hold this, please? Here it is...

215
00:13:41,517 --> 00:13:44,825
Dwight Ramos in three, two, one!

216
00:13:47,128 --> 00:13:49,197
MVP, Mother!

217
00:13:49,197 --> 00:13:51,499
Thanks! Bye!

218
00:13:51,499 --> 00:13:53,134
Let's go here, Mother!

219
00:13:54,502 --> 00:13:56,783
Father, they also have
something different here.

220
00:13:56,783 --> 00:14:00,642
They have a great wall of climbing.

221
00:14:00,642 --> 00:14:02,510
<i>Mother, I'll try it out.</i>

222
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:04,408
<i>Just stay there and watch.</i>

223
00:14:14,877 --> 00:14:18,393
Mother, Father, I can't do it.

224
00:14:18,393 --> 00:14:20,128
The library is beautiful.

225
00:14:20,128 --> 00:14:21,696
If only we have this kind of library,

226
00:14:21,696 --> 00:14:23,665
I can live here for the rest of my life.

227
00:14:23,665 --> 00:14:27,587
I will read every day and, Mother, look.

228
00:14:27,587 --> 00:14:29,737
They have a book about how to raise a llama,

229
00:14:29,737 --> 00:14:31,923
<i>when I don't even know what a llama is.</i>

230
00:14:31,923 --> 00:14:34,197
It looks like a mix of goat and giraffe.

231
00:14:34,197 --> 00:14:35,276
I don't know that.

232
00:14:35,276 --> 00:14:38,462
Only a fool will not read in a library
as beautiful as this.

233
00:14:38,462 --> 00:14:40,882
Mother, there are a lot of books.

234
00:14:40,882 --> 00:14:44,392
Mother, Father, this is one of
the famous places I see in GU.

235
00:14:44,392 --> 00:14:47,822
Before, I only see this online,
but now here it is.

236
00:14:47,822 --> 00:14:49,257
Tada...

237
00:14:49,257 --> 00:14:51,359
It's the fountain!

238
00:14:53,394 --> 00:14:55,830
The water is cold, Mother.

239
00:15:02,403 --> 00:15:04,656
You know, Mother, Father,

240
00:15:04,656 --> 00:15:09,277
there's a part in my heart that's sad
because I wasn't able to study here.

241
00:15:09,277 --> 00:15:14,115
But half of my heart is excited
because next year,

242
00:15:14,115 --> 00:15:17,852
I will try again to apply
so I can get into this school.

243
00:15:17,852 --> 00:15:21,790
I will try again to fulfill all our dreams.

244
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:25,493
<i>Mother, Father, join me, please.</i>

245
00:15:26,327 --> 00:15:31,266
And I promise you,
I will fulfill all of our dreams.

246
00:15:31,266 --> 00:15:32,901
Everything.

247
00:15:32,901 --> 00:15:37,005
And I will never get tired of dreaming.

248
00:15:37,005 --> 00:15:39,974
You don't have to promise, Florence,

249
00:15:39,974 --> 00:15:42,544
because your father and I believe

250
00:15:42,544 --> 00:15:46,114
that you will fulfill
everything you want in life.

251
00:15:46,114 --> 00:15:48,750
We're always here to support you.

252
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:52,253
Oh, Father, Mother, wait.
Mr. Dencio is calling.

253
00:15:52,253 --> 00:15:53,454
Maybe he's looking for me.

254
00:15:53,454 --> 00:15:54,622
Bye for now.

255
00:15:54,622 --> 00:15:57,024
I love you, Mother, I love you, Father.

256
00:15:58,993 --> 00:16:00,775
Mr. Dencio...

257
00:16:01,996 --> 00:16:03,731
Hello, Mr. Dencio?

258
00:16:03,731 --> 00:16:06,010
Hello, Florence.

259
00:16:06,010 --> 00:16:07,502
Where are you?

260
00:16:07,502 --> 00:16:09,863
Don Ferell has been looking for you
for a while now.

261
00:16:09,863 --> 00:16:11,409
Is that so?

262
00:16:11,409 --> 00:16:13,808
Okay, I'm on my way back.

263
00:16:13,808 --> 00:16:15,843
Wait, Mr. Dencio!

264
00:16:18,046 --> 00:16:20,048
Grandpa Garp, I'm sorry.

265
00:16:20,048 --> 00:16:21,535
I lost track of time.

266
00:16:21,535 --> 00:16:23,418
I just went for a stroll in the area.

267
00:16:23,418 --> 00:16:25,353
GU is so beautiful, that's why,

268
00:16:25,353 --> 00:16:27,956
I couldn't stop myself
from enjoying the area.

269
00:16:27,956 --> 00:16:29,791
I also took a video call
with my mother and father,

270
00:16:29,791 --> 00:16:31,762
because it's always been my dream
to get into this school.

271
00:16:31,762 --> 00:16:34,295
- It's so beautiful...
- Florence, please stop.

272
00:16:34,295 --> 00:16:35,530
You have to relax,

273
00:16:35,530 --> 00:16:38,867
because I have something important
to tell you.

274
00:16:38,867 --> 00:16:39,901
What's that?

275
00:16:39,901 --> 00:16:41,371
Did I do something wrong?

276
00:16:41,371 --> 00:16:43,706
Nothing. You didn't do anything wrong.

277
00:16:44,405 --> 00:16:46,908
Dean, this is Florence Dela Cruz.

278
00:16:46,908 --> 00:16:48,743
Florence, this is Dean Alvaro.

279
00:16:48,743 --> 00:16:50,345
- Hello, Florence.
- Hello...

280
00:16:50,345 --> 00:16:52,986
It's my pleasure to finally meet you.

281
00:16:52,986 --> 00:16:56,568
We never get the chance
to know each other personally.

282
00:16:57,418 --> 00:17:00,388
But I already know you,
Ms. Florence Dela Cruz,

283
00:17:00,388 --> 00:17:04,370
because I personally reviewed and approved

284
00:17:04,370 --> 00:17:06,494
your application for a scholarship.

285
00:17:06,494 --> 00:17:08,563
- What?
- Yes.

286
00:17:08,563 --> 00:17:12,333
Actually, Florence,
I had your background checked.

287
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:13,968
Excuse me, Don Ferell,

288
00:17:13,968 --> 00:17:18,526
here is the background check
that we did for our new cook.

289
00:17:18,526 --> 00:17:21,628
All information about her is there.

290
00:17:22,449 --> 00:17:24,484
Very bright student.

291
00:17:26,273 --> 00:17:28,675
Always gets the top honors...

292
00:17:29,571 --> 00:17:34,342
She even got a scholarship at GU.

293
00:17:38,885 --> 00:17:43,496
Don't take it personally that Serafica
did a background check on you.

294
00:17:43,496 --> 00:17:47,535
That's standard for every new employee
who will enter our family.

295
00:17:47,535 --> 00:17:51,339
The safety of my grandsons is paramount,

296
00:17:51,339 --> 00:17:53,474
but when I was reviewing your information,

297
00:17:53,474 --> 00:17:56,733
I saw the scholarship status
in the university.

298
00:17:56,733 --> 00:17:58,880
That's why, I talked to Dean.

299
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,114
I'm sorry, Florence,

300
00:18:00,114 --> 00:18:04,752
but I took the liberty of explaining
to Don Ferell your situation.

301
00:18:04,752 --> 00:18:08,536
After all, he's one of the board members
of this university

302
00:18:08,536 --> 00:18:13,761
and one of the biggest donors
in our Honors Program.

303
00:18:13,761 --> 00:18:15,096
According to Dean,

304
00:18:15,096 --> 00:18:18,433
you turned down the scholarship
because you needed to work

305
00:18:18,433 --> 00:18:25,139
to help your father who, if I'm not mistaken,
have a heart problem.

306
00:18:25,773 --> 00:18:28,676
Yes but he's doing okay now.

307
00:18:28,676 --> 00:18:30,745
Yeah, but it still bothers me.

308
00:18:30,745 --> 00:18:33,918
Sadly, an intelligent,

309
00:18:33,918 --> 00:18:39,163
hardworking, and good student like you
is not in school.

310
00:18:39,163 --> 00:18:42,980
That's why... I have a proposal for you.

311
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:46,949
You can still cook for us,
to help your family,

312
00:18:46,949 --> 00:18:54,369
but now you have the option to study in GU,
if you want.

313
00:19:01,709 --> 00:19:02,871
Really, Florence?

314
00:19:02,871 --> 00:19:05,012
That's great news.

315
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,182
Are you sure about what Don Ferell said,

316
00:19:08,182 --> 00:19:10,018
that he'll allow you to study
at the university

317
00:19:10,018 --> 00:19:11,865
while working in their household as a cook?

318
00:19:11,865 --> 00:19:15,656
I also can't believe it,
but that's what Grandpa Garp said.

319
00:19:15,656 --> 00:19:17,584
Grandpa Garp?

320
00:19:17,584 --> 00:19:20,462
<i>That's what Don Ferell wants to be called.</i>

321
00:19:20,462 --> 00:19:23,396
Wow, and you're calling him Grandpa Garp too.

322
00:19:23,396 --> 00:19:24,766
Maybe tomorrow and the day after,

323
00:19:24,766 --> 00:19:27,301
you'll become a grandchild of Grandpa Garp.

324
00:19:27,301 --> 00:19:28,403
But, my child,

325
00:19:28,403 --> 00:19:31,873
can you manage to work and study
at the same time?

326
00:19:31,873 --> 00:19:33,941
Won't you have a hard time?

327
00:19:33,941 --> 00:19:37,933
Grandpa Garp's grandsons
are also studying in that school.

328
00:19:37,933 --> 00:19:41,215
So if they're in school,
I don't have someone to cook for.

329
00:19:41,215 --> 00:19:44,398
And the Dean also allowed me
not to take a full load of my first semester

330
00:19:44,398 --> 00:19:47,522
so my schedule is lighter.

331
00:19:47,522 --> 00:19:49,623
But your mother has a point.

332
00:19:49,623 --> 00:19:53,917
You might exhaust yourself
and won't have time for yourself.

333
00:19:53,917 --> 00:19:56,964
<i>No, don't worry. I can handle that.</i>

334
00:19:56,964 --> 00:20:00,101
<i>I, of all people, inherited your good traits.</i>

335
00:20:00,101 --> 00:20:04,572
Just make sure that you can
take care of yourself.

336
00:20:04,572 --> 00:20:07,642
Yes, Mother.
I promise that you don't have to worry

337
00:20:07,642 --> 00:20:08,876
because I can do this.

338
00:20:08,876 --> 00:20:11,964
Okay, your father needs to rest,

339
00:20:11,964 --> 00:20:15,016
and it's his turn to take care of himself.

340
00:20:15,016 --> 00:20:16,913
Goodnight, my child.

341
00:20:16,913 --> 00:20:18,726
I'm so happy for you.

342
00:20:18,726 --> 00:20:20,555
I'm so happy too.

343
00:20:20,555 --> 00:20:22,321
Goodnight, Mother. Goodnight, Father.

344
00:20:22,321 --> 00:20:25,624
I love you both. I miss you.

345
00:20:29,063 --> 00:20:30,965
Just a second.

346
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:41,194
Owen?

347
00:20:43,897 --> 00:20:47,381
Florence, I heard the good news.

348
00:20:47,381 --> 00:20:48,549
Why don't we celebrate?

349
00:20:48,549 --> 00:20:49,976
Celebrate?

350
00:20:49,976 --> 00:20:51,452
We'll drink?

351
00:20:51,452 --> 00:20:53,132
I don't drink.

352
00:20:53,132 --> 00:20:55,811
Who said we'll be drinking?

353
00:20:59,994 --> 00:21:02,163
What's happening here?

354
00:21:02,163 --> 00:21:04,147
Surprise.

355
00:21:08,765 --> 00:21:11,606
I actually was the first to hear
the good news.

356
00:21:11,606 --> 00:21:15,342
I overheard Grandpa Garp
and Ms. Serafica talking...

357
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:19,947
I heard about his plans
of letting you study in GU.

358
00:21:20,715 --> 00:21:23,384
Don't worry, Florence.

359
00:21:23,384 --> 00:21:25,410
Troy is already a good boy.

360
00:21:25,410 --> 00:21:27,187
Right, Troy?

361
00:21:30,665 --> 00:21:32,126
Really?

362
00:21:32,126 --> 00:21:34,908
- Here.
- Thank you.

363
00:21:36,164 --> 00:21:39,658
I'm also looking for a chance
to apologize to you.

364
00:21:39,658 --> 00:21:41,035
I was one of the guys who played a prank

365
00:21:41,035 --> 00:21:43,404
on your first day here in the mansion.

366
00:21:44,305 --> 00:21:46,507
That's okay, forget about it.

367
00:21:46,507 --> 00:21:48,910
I already forgot about it.

368
00:21:48,910 --> 00:21:50,944
What happened that day?

369
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:55,816
Don't do that, never forget.

370
00:21:55,816 --> 00:21:58,623
Or we'll keep doing our mistakes
from the past.

371
00:21:58,623 --> 00:22:00,778
We must learn from history.

372
00:22:00,778 --> 00:22:07,328
I, Aldus, and Tristan
were being jerks that day.

373
00:22:07,328 --> 00:22:09,565
I feel really bad about it.

374
00:22:10,331 --> 00:22:13,568
I hope I'll be okay with Tristan and Aldus,

375
00:22:13,568 --> 00:22:18,005
and Nero too,
so I'll be cool with all the Ferells.

376
00:22:18,773 --> 00:22:21,375
Isn't Nero okay with you?

377
00:22:22,143 --> 00:22:23,623
Nero?

378
00:22:23,623 --> 00:22:26,013
He's okay with me?

379
00:22:26,013 --> 00:22:29,041
He always gives me dagger looks.

380
00:22:29,041 --> 00:22:33,788
No way. He only looks mad,
but he's okay with you.

381
00:22:33,788 --> 00:22:35,323
As a matter of fact,

382
00:22:35,323 --> 00:22:38,392
he's one of your biggest defenders
here in the mansion.

383
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:42,162
- Nero?
- Yes.

384
00:22:42,162 --> 00:22:44,331
My biggest defender?

385
00:22:45,302 --> 00:22:47,668
How did that happen?

386
00:22:47,668 --> 00:22:50,670
If you're enjoying at the expense of others,

387
00:22:50,670 --> 00:22:52,940
that's not called fun.

388
00:22:52,940 --> 00:22:56,310
You call that disrespectful.

389
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:58,379
Who are you? Are you her boyfriend?

390
00:22:58,379 --> 00:23:02,083
Hey... Do I have to be her boyfriend
just to tell you

391
00:23:02,083 --> 00:23:03,851
what you're doing is wrong?

392
00:23:03,851 --> 00:23:07,051
It was he who confronted us
to stop us from playing a prank on you.

393
00:23:07,051 --> 00:23:09,613
Oh, really?

394
00:23:09,613 --> 00:23:10,996
Yes.

395
00:23:14,862 --> 00:23:16,630
And not only that,

396
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:20,343
he was the first one to show support
for your cooking.

397
00:23:20,343 --> 00:23:23,655
What do you think
of Florence's home cooked dish?

398
00:23:24,605 --> 00:23:28,208
Is it good or should I fire her?

399
00:23:31,564 --> 00:23:37,657
Because I won't force you
if you really don't like it,

400
00:23:37,657 --> 00:23:38,853
there's nothing we can do.

401
00:23:38,853 --> 00:23:42,356
But it's you who will decide.

402
00:23:42,356 --> 00:23:44,604
It's you who will judge.

403
00:23:44,604 --> 00:23:46,479
What do you say?

404
00:23:48,277 --> 00:23:50,120
I like her...

405
00:23:51,232 --> 00:23:54,683
I mean, I like her cooking.

406
00:23:56,771 --> 00:24:00,574
And if I can have it my way,
I want her to stay as our cook.

407
00:24:00,574 --> 00:24:03,210
That's good.

408
00:24:04,345 --> 00:24:06,180
- You're right.
- I agree with you, Nero.

409
00:24:06,180 --> 00:24:08,615
The food is delicious.

410
00:24:10,318 --> 00:24:12,286
If I'm being honest,

411
00:24:12,286 --> 00:24:16,056
I would've voted for you too,
but Nero got ahead of me.

412
00:24:17,391 --> 00:24:20,552
Just say you got scared
because you're afraid...

413
00:24:20,552 --> 00:24:24,398
that Aldus and Tristan will pick on you.

414
00:24:24,398 --> 00:24:28,618
But we can't deny the fact that
it was Nero who first talked.

415
00:24:28,618 --> 00:24:31,939
He was the first who showed support
for your cooking.

416
00:24:31,939 --> 00:24:35,209
And we all know that
Nero is Grandpa's favorite,

417
00:24:35,209 --> 00:24:37,613
that's why, when he said
that he likes your cooking,

418
00:24:37,613 --> 00:24:40,514
well, no one's going to challenge that.

419
00:24:41,527 --> 00:24:44,184
It's also not a stretch
to say that because of Nero,

420
00:24:44,184 --> 00:24:47,433
up to now,
you're still the cook for the Ferells.

421
00:24:47,433 --> 00:24:52,025
Because if not for him, you're already fired.

422
00:25:24,492 --> 00:25:26,660
Do you think I'm scared of you?

423
00:25:26,660 --> 00:25:29,196
I'm not scared of the Ferell brothers

424
00:25:29,196 --> 00:25:31,966
and I don't care no matter who you are.

425
00:25:31,966 --> 00:25:33,569
Is that so?

426
00:25:33,569 --> 00:25:36,799
Project eliminate Florence Dela Cruz,
activated.

427
00:25:36,799 --> 00:25:39,874
Ferell brothers, let's go!

428
00:25:39,874 --> 00:25:41,208
Hey, what's with you.

429
00:25:41,208 --> 00:25:44,111
Ouch! What are you doing?

430
00:25:44,111 --> 00:25:46,647
Get your hands off me. Ouch! What's with you?

431
00:25:46,647 --> 00:25:49,483
Let me go!

432
00:26:10,371 --> 00:26:14,408
Thank you, Nero, thank you for saving me.

433
00:26:14,408 --> 00:26:18,078
Thank you for choosing me over your brothers.

434
00:26:37,264 --> 00:26:40,734
What's this again, Florence?

435
00:26:40,734 --> 00:26:44,071
Stop this madness.

436
00:26:44,071 --> 00:26:48,409
You've been thinking a lot of nonsense,

437
00:26:48,409 --> 00:26:51,448
that's why, you're dreaming such things.

438
00:26:52,346 --> 00:26:55,901
You're getting too much affected
by the Ferells.

439
00:27:00,454 --> 00:27:03,958
<i>We can't deny the fact that
it was Nero who first talked.</i>

440
00:27:03,958 --> 00:27:07,261
<i>He was the first who showed support
for your cooking.</i>

441
00:27:07,261 --> 00:27:10,297
And we all know that
Nero is Grandpa's favorite,

442
00:27:10,297 --> 00:27:12,600
that's why, when he said
that he likes your cooking,

443
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:16,537
well, no one's going to challenge that.

444
00:27:16,537 --> 00:27:19,240
It's also not a stretch to say
that because of Nero,

445
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:22,543
up to now,
you're still the cook for the Ferells.

446
00:27:22,543 --> 00:27:27,014
<i>Because if not for him, you're already fired.</i>

447
00:27:30,932 --> 00:27:33,869
Sorry, Nero, for judging you.

448
00:27:34,555 --> 00:27:37,824
You're okay even if you're a bit weird.

449
00:27:39,159 --> 00:27:43,461
Okay, promise, I will not judge you again.

450
00:28:15,029 --> 00:28:17,765
What's with you, Florence,
you get scared easily.

451
00:28:17,765 --> 00:28:19,900
You better wake up.

452
00:28:32,446 --> 00:28:33,447
Just calm down.

453
00:28:33,447 --> 00:28:35,482
It's just me.

454
00:28:37,230 --> 00:28:39,587
Why do you look that way?

455
00:28:39,587 --> 00:28:42,823
This is part of my skincare process.

456
00:28:42,823 --> 00:28:45,759
It's difficult to maintain my glowing skin.

457
00:28:45,759 --> 00:28:47,261
Too much pressure,

458
00:28:47,261 --> 00:28:48,529
especially since a lot of people is saying

459
00:28:48,529 --> 00:28:51,965
I look so much like Gretchen Barretto.

460
00:28:54,101 --> 00:28:55,235
What?

461
00:28:55,235 --> 00:28:56,323
That's beside the point.

462
00:28:56,323 --> 00:28:59,707
My point is why are you up early?

463
00:28:59,707 --> 00:29:02,042
Bad dream?

464
00:29:03,277 --> 00:29:05,779
Not really, I just jolted out of sleep,

465
00:29:05,779 --> 00:29:08,610
and in a few hours, the sun will be up.

466
00:29:08,610 --> 00:29:12,393
I thought of starting work early.

467
00:29:12,393 --> 00:29:15,154
Well then let me take this opportunity

468
00:29:15,154 --> 00:29:18,440
to tell you that Don Ferell and I
talked already

469
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:21,362
about sending you to school.

470
00:29:21,362 --> 00:29:24,064
I was planning to talk to you.

471
00:29:24,064 --> 00:29:27,646
I just want to let you know that even though
I'll be going to GU,

472
00:29:27,646 --> 00:29:30,937
I will not neglect my work here.

473
00:29:31,703 --> 00:29:36,594
Very good then,
I guess we won't have a problem.

474
00:29:53,661 --> 00:29:55,051
Nero?

475
00:29:56,012 --> 00:29:58,532
He's early.

476
00:29:58,532 --> 00:30:00,567
Where is he going?

477
00:30:46,378 --> 00:30:48,413
How are you?

478
00:30:49,471 --> 00:30:51,372
Are you hungry?

479
00:30:52,379 --> 00:30:53,951
Here.

480
00:30:53,951 --> 00:30:56,160
Just eat up.

481
00:31:03,909 --> 00:31:05,535
Is that not enough?

482
00:31:09,103 --> 00:31:14,208
Hey, you, I thought a ghost is scaring me,
but it's just you.

483
00:31:14,208 --> 00:31:16,777
Never ever give up.

484
00:31:16,777 --> 00:31:19,112
You can do this.

485
00:31:22,683 --> 00:31:25,023
Doves?

486
00:31:25,023 --> 00:31:26,620
It's you again?

487
00:31:26,620 --> 00:31:29,356
You even woke me up.

488
00:31:35,099 --> 00:31:37,537
Don't get tired of dreaming.

489
00:31:39,842 --> 00:31:43,268
He's the one sending me messages?

490
00:31:43,268 --> 00:31:45,470
Do you want music?

491
00:31:46,607 --> 00:31:49,509
Do you want some music? Okay.

492
00:31:59,470 --> 00:32:01,065
There you go.

493
00:32:05,926 --> 00:32:07,971
Join me.

494
00:33:05,731 --> 00:33:07,269
Who's there?

495
00:33:12,329 --> 00:33:13,918
Who's there?

496
00:33:17,097 --> 00:33:18,868
Who's there?

497
00:33:24,942 --> 00:33:27,410
It's just you.

498
00:33:29,333 --> 00:33:30,867
Come here.

499
00:33:32,779 --> 00:33:33,754
I've been looking for you.

500
00:33:33,754 --> 00:33:36,261
I thought you were preyed on by other birds.

501
00:33:37,184 --> 00:33:38,785
You're hungry already?

502
00:33:38,785 --> 00:33:41,921
Come here, I will feed you.

503
00:33:43,503 --> 00:33:45,926
It's just you, I thought it was someone else.

504
00:33:45,926 --> 00:33:47,987
Come here.

505
00:33:49,525 --> 00:33:51,698
Hey, you, I miss you.

506
00:33:52,566 --> 00:33:54,567
You haven't eaten yet, right?

507
00:34:01,441 --> 00:34:03,443
It's you again?

508
00:34:03,443 --> 00:34:05,445
You even woke me up.

509
00:34:18,659 --> 00:34:20,928
Don't get tired of dreaming.

510
00:34:20,928 --> 00:34:25,145
So it was Nero who was sending me
those secret messages?

511
00:34:29,778 --> 00:34:32,072
He is defending me.

512
00:34:32,072 --> 00:34:34,474
He only looks mad, but he's okay with you.

513
00:34:34,474 --> 00:34:35,943
As a matter of fact,

514
00:34:35,943 --> 00:34:38,645
he's one of your biggest defenders
here in the mansion.

515
00:34:38,645 --> 00:34:42,649
He confronted us to stop picking on you.

516
00:34:42,649 --> 00:34:45,519
He also wants my cooking.

517
00:34:45,519 --> 00:34:49,823
Because of Nero, up to now,
you're still the cook for the Ferells.

518
00:34:49,823 --> 00:34:54,663
Because if not for him,
you're probably fired by now.

519
00:34:55,362 --> 00:34:59,540
And he sends me a message using a dove.

520
00:35:01,634 --> 00:35:02,836
Hey, you.

521
00:35:02,836 --> 00:35:06,640
I thought a ghost is scaring me
when it was just you.

522
00:35:06,640 --> 00:35:09,331
Never ever give up.

523
00:35:09,331 --> 00:35:11,110
You can do it.

524
00:35:12,878 --> 00:35:14,446
What's that?

525
00:35:15,148 --> 00:35:19,219
He likes me, as in...

526
00:35:19,219 --> 00:35:21,888
he wants me to be his girlfriend, is that it?

527
00:35:31,740 --> 00:35:33,342
So?

528
00:35:34,068 --> 00:35:35,429
What will the grandsons have?

529
00:35:35,429 --> 00:35:37,167
Adobong Kalapati.

530
00:35:37,167 --> 00:35:38,900
Is this a joke?

531
00:35:38,901 --> 00:35:41,975
No, I mean I'll be cooking adobado.

532
00:35:41,975 --> 00:35:44,320
Adobado?

533
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:46,571
Do you mean Adobo?

534
00:35:46,571 --> 00:35:48,734
- Well?
- Yes.

535
00:35:49,554 --> 00:35:52,619
Okay, just make sure
you'll cook for Dencio too.

536
00:35:59,860 --> 00:36:01,461
Adobo.

537
00:36:04,331 --> 00:36:05,532
Adobado...

538
00:36:05,532 --> 00:36:08,073
Adobo.

539
00:36:14,974 --> 00:36:17,219
Go ahead and eat, sir.

540
00:36:17,219 --> 00:36:18,645
Don't call me sir.

541
00:36:18,645 --> 00:36:20,173
Just Nero.

542
00:36:21,214 --> 00:36:25,152
Okay, sir, I mean Nero.

543
00:36:25,152 --> 00:36:27,387
This looks delicious.

544
00:36:27,387 --> 00:36:29,122
I'm hungry.

545
00:36:31,649 --> 00:36:33,460
Florence, why don't you join us?

546
00:36:33,460 --> 00:36:37,864
No, thank you, Grandpa Garp.
I promised Mr. Dencio I'll be joining them.

547
00:36:37,864 --> 00:36:41,773
Have you talked to Serafica
about your scholarship at the university?

548
00:36:41,773 --> 00:36:43,503
Yes, everything is okay.

549
00:36:43,503 --> 00:36:45,272
That's very good.

550
00:36:45,272 --> 00:36:46,873
You're in your freshman year in college,
Florence,

551
00:36:46,873 --> 00:36:48,206
so we're just the same.

552
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:49,645
What's your department?

553
00:36:49,645 --> 00:36:50,770
Com Arts.

554
00:36:50,770 --> 00:36:51,912
Com Arts?

555
00:36:51,912 --> 00:36:53,213
It's fun there.

556
00:36:53,213 --> 00:36:55,857
Nero likes people from Com Arts.

557
00:36:57,584 --> 00:36:59,453
Don't tease Florence.

558
00:36:59,453 --> 00:37:02,122
And, Florence, you better be careful.

559
00:37:02,122 --> 00:37:06,943
If you see Nero in the Com Arts building,
you better hide.

560
00:37:08,428 --> 00:37:10,530
I don't think it's a good joke, Tristan.

561
00:37:10,530 --> 00:37:12,632
We're making things awkward for Florence.

562
00:37:12,632 --> 00:37:14,412
No, Owen, it's okay.

563
00:37:14,412 --> 00:37:17,202
Besides, I'm not fond of the Ferells.

564
00:37:17,202 --> 00:37:20,004
Oh, burn.

565
00:37:23,189 --> 00:37:26,345
But, Nero, you already have an advantage.

566
00:37:32,352 --> 00:37:35,322
Because if there's someone you like
from Com Arts Department,

567
00:37:35,322 --> 00:37:37,256
I can act as a bridge.

568
00:37:38,825 --> 00:37:41,476
Oh.

569
00:37:43,096 --> 00:37:45,431
Why don't you act as a bridge for each other?

570
00:37:47,968 --> 00:37:49,636
Sure.

571
00:37:49,636 --> 00:37:52,271
Perfect, there's someone I like.

572
00:37:55,876 --> 00:37:58,778
"Sure. Perfect, there's someone I like."

573
00:37:58,778 --> 00:38:02,149
What? Are we going to eat
or we'll discuss Nero's love life?

574
00:38:02,149 --> 00:38:03,483
Aldus is right.

575
00:38:03,483 --> 00:38:07,487
Let's eat before this delicious dish
Florence cooked gets cold.

576
00:38:07,487 --> 00:38:09,589
Let's go, guys.

577
00:38:09,589 --> 00:38:10,944
Go!

578
00:38:17,335 --> 00:38:19,866
Florence, let's eat.

579
00:38:19,866 --> 00:38:23,603
Mr. Dencio, you know that whenever I cook,
I always taste the food.

580
00:38:23,603 --> 00:38:26,501
That's why after cooking, I'm already full.

581
00:38:27,507 --> 00:38:29,576
So, you have no appetite.

582
00:38:29,576 --> 00:38:33,079
Oh my, I might think that you're in love.

583
00:38:33,079 --> 00:38:37,495
It's the opposite,
when I'm in love, the more I eat.

584
00:38:37,495 --> 00:38:38,785
Why?

585
00:38:38,785 --> 00:38:41,254
Have you been in love?

586
00:38:41,254 --> 00:38:43,256
Yes, of course.

587
00:38:43,256 --> 00:38:45,058
Oh, really?

588
00:38:45,058 --> 00:38:46,259
You're still young.

589
00:38:46,259 --> 00:38:49,529
And if you've been in love before,
when and to whom?

590
00:38:50,274 --> 00:38:52,199
- That's right.
- I'm in love every day

591
00:38:52,199 --> 00:38:55,001
because I love my mother and father.

592
00:38:55,001 --> 00:38:57,771
- I love my family so much.
- No wonder.

593
00:38:57,771 --> 00:39:00,039
Good answer.

594
00:39:00,740 --> 00:39:06,079
Speaking of... I'll just call my parents...

595
00:39:06,079 --> 00:39:08,581
the people I love in my life.

596
00:39:09,549 --> 00:39:11,584
Hello, Mother, Father.

597
00:39:14,854 --> 00:39:16,456
<i>Hello, Florence!</i>

598
00:39:16,456 --> 00:39:19,638
Your mother and I were thinking,

599
00:39:19,638 --> 00:39:22,195
what gift can we give Don Ferell

600
00:39:22,195 --> 00:39:25,133
for his kindness to you as a thank you gift.

601
00:39:25,133 --> 00:39:27,901
<i>That's why we thought of
giving him a gift certificate.</i>

602
00:39:27,901 --> 00:39:29,536
<i>Oh, how about a teddy bear?</i>

603
00:39:29,536 --> 00:39:32,772
Or small cars for his small grandsons?

604
00:39:32,772 --> 00:39:34,541
Yes.

605
00:39:34,541 --> 00:39:37,210
Mother, Father, that's not needed anymore.

606
00:39:37,210 --> 00:39:38,345
Are you sure?

607
00:39:38,345 --> 00:39:41,081
I'm worried about these gift certificates,
they might expire.

608
00:39:41,081 --> 00:39:42,282
Mother, Father,

609
00:39:42,282 --> 00:39:44,584
there's nothing we can give
that Grandpa Garp needs.

610
00:39:44,584 --> 00:39:48,910
Maybe you've forgotten,
he owns half of our town.

611
00:39:50,440 --> 00:39:51,791
How about a soul?

612
00:39:51,791 --> 00:39:52,859
Does he need a soul?

613
00:39:52,859 --> 00:39:54,559
Ours are available.

614
00:39:54,559 --> 00:39:56,162
You're full of jokes.

615
00:39:56,162 --> 00:39:57,631
Okay, why don't we do this, Florence?

616
00:39:57,631 --> 00:40:00,066
If you can think of anything
that the mansion needs

617
00:40:00,066 --> 00:40:03,363
that your father and I can give,
just let us know.

618
00:40:03,363 --> 00:40:08,240
So we can give something
as a token of gratitude

619
00:40:08,240 --> 00:40:10,644
for the Ferells' kindness to you.

620
00:40:10,644 --> 00:40:11,845
Yes, Mother.

621
00:40:11,845 --> 00:40:12,846
<i>How about you?</i>

622
00:40:12,846 --> 00:40:14,481
<i>How are you doing there?</i>

623
00:40:14,481 --> 00:40:16,559
<i>Yes, is there a new rumor?</i>

624
00:40:16,559 --> 00:40:18,718
Nothing much but...

625
00:40:18,718 --> 00:40:20,120
<i>But what?</i>

626
00:40:20,120 --> 00:40:22,088
Is that Serafica treating you badly?

627
00:40:22,088 --> 00:40:25,058
Just tell me and I'll confront that witch.

628
00:40:25,058 --> 00:40:28,862
No, Mother,
there's just something I want to ask you.

629
00:40:28,862 --> 00:40:31,998
Florence, how many times
should I explain to you

630
00:40:31,998 --> 00:40:35,135
that the sun is the center
of the solar system

631
00:40:35,135 --> 00:40:38,074
and moving around it are the planets...

632
00:40:39,566 --> 00:40:40,640
Just take it easy...

633
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:41,974
Hold on.

634
00:40:41,974 --> 00:40:45,378
- Here, water first.
- Father, are you okay?

635
00:40:45,378 --> 00:40:48,138
<i>Yes, he's doing okay, Florence.</i>

636
00:40:48,138 --> 00:40:51,885
Don't worry, Father,
my question is not about the solar system.

637
00:40:51,885 --> 00:40:53,953
It's just about...

638
00:40:54,921 --> 00:40:56,656
about my friend.

639
00:40:57,757 --> 00:40:59,392
Who's that friend of yours?

640
00:40:59,392 --> 00:41:01,294
It's Jenny.

641
00:41:01,294 --> 00:41:02,429
<i>Jenny?</i>

642
00:41:02,429 --> 00:41:03,430
Jennylyn?

643
00:41:03,430 --> 00:41:04,698
Jennylyn Mercado?

644
00:41:04,698 --> 00:41:06,966
You're now friends with Jennylyn Mercado?

645
00:41:06,966 --> 00:41:08,968
No, it's not Jennylyn Mercado...

646
00:41:08,968 --> 00:41:10,537
It's Jenny.

647
00:41:10,537 --> 00:41:13,773
Never mind, you're just making
a fool out of me.

648
00:41:13,773 --> 00:41:15,475
It's your fault,
you're fooling your daughter.

649
00:41:15,475 --> 00:41:16,676
No, go ahead, Florence.

650
00:41:16,676 --> 00:41:18,978
What's the problem with
that Jennylyn Mercado,

651
00:41:18,978 --> 00:41:21,614
I mean, Jenny.

652
00:41:21,614 --> 00:41:26,986
Well, it's because someone
is sending her secret messages.

653
00:41:26,986 --> 00:41:28,755
Are these obscene pictures?

654
00:41:28,755 --> 00:41:31,758
No, Father, these are just ordinary messages,

655
00:41:31,758 --> 00:41:34,828
something like words of wisdom.

656
00:41:34,828 --> 00:41:37,831
It's inspiring and makes you feel better.

657
00:41:37,831 --> 00:41:39,899
What's the problem?

658
00:41:39,899 --> 00:41:46,672
She discovered the person
who is sending those secret messages.

659
00:41:47,807 --> 00:41:49,476
What will she do?

660
00:41:49,476 --> 00:41:51,578
Should she confront the person?

661
00:41:51,578 --> 00:41:55,081
Should she talk to the person
and ask why he's doing that?

662
00:41:55,081 --> 00:42:00,086
Why is he sending her messages
if he has a secret motive?

663
00:42:00,086 --> 00:42:01,857
A secret desire?

664
00:42:01,857 --> 00:42:02,921
You know, Florence,

665
00:42:02,921 --> 00:42:06,361
there's only one thing your father and I
can say about that.

666
00:42:07,360 --> 00:42:09,762
Bring it to DJ Acapulco.

667
00:42:14,134 --> 00:42:17,570
<i>Good Morning to our listeners and viewers,</i>

668
00:42:17,570 --> 00:42:21,064
<i>because we are simulcast live via UTobe.</i>

669
00:42:21,064 --> 00:42:25,745
<i>And thank you to the 55,000 concurrent views,</i>

670
00:42:25,745 --> 00:42:26,780
<i>that's awesome.</i>

671
00:42:26,780 --> 00:42:29,574
<i>Perfect to start our program.</i>

672
00:42:29,574 --> 00:42:34,954
<i>So, for our first messenger,
what is your favorite color?</i>

673
00:42:34,954 --> 00:42:38,465
<i>The question is so corny,
but of course, Fuschia.</i>

674
00:42:38,465 --> 00:42:40,360
<i>But if you'll ask me how to spell it,
never mind.</i>

675
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:43,863
<i>I'll just say red. Anyway,
let's go to our second message.</i>

676
00:42:43,863 --> 00:42:47,366
<i>Her question is interesting.</i>

677
00:42:47,366 --> 00:42:51,547
<i>Will I confront the person
who is sending me secret messages?</i>

678
00:42:51,547 --> 00:42:54,307
<i>The messages are actually sweet and nice.</i>

679
00:42:54,307 --> 00:42:59,250
<i>And should he know that I know
that he's sending me secret messages?</i>

680
00:42:59,250 --> 00:43:01,547
<i>From Jenny.</i>

681
00:43:01,547 --> 00:43:04,918
<i>Could Jennylyn Mercado send this message?</i>

682
00:43:04,918 --> 00:43:07,844
<i>I'm pretty sure she has
a lot of secret admirers.</i>

683
00:43:07,844 --> 00:43:10,123
<i>Anyway, you know, Jenny,</i>

684
00:43:10,123 --> 00:43:14,125
<i>some people are having a hard time
showing their feelings.</i>

685
00:43:14,125 --> 00:43:18,729
<i>That's why sometimes,
some resort to secret messages.</i>

686
00:43:18,729 --> 00:43:23,432
<i>And what I can advise you is,
don't confront him yet.</i>

687
00:43:23,432 --> 00:43:27,191
<i>Give him time and eventually,</i>

688
00:43:27,191 --> 00:43:31,939
<i>he will have the courage to face you</i>

689
00:43:31,939 --> 00:43:35,484
<i>and tell what he truly feels for you.</i>

690
00:43:35,484 --> 00:43:37,950
<i>And when the time is right,</i>

691
00:43:37,950 --> 00:43:42,984
<i>he will personally shout out to the world
his love for you.</i>

692
00:43:42,984 --> 00:43:48,561
<i>But for now,
just let him secretly express his feelings</i>

693
00:43:48,561 --> 00:43:51,397
<i>through secret messages.</i>

694
00:43:51,397 --> 00:43:53,199
There you go,

695
00:43:53,199 --> 00:44:00,751
Jennylyn Mercado just needs time
and a chance for her secret admirer.

696
00:44:00,751 --> 00:44:08,481
I disagree because I understand
what Jennylyn Mercado is going through.

697
00:44:08,481 --> 00:44:11,791
If that's how truly he feels about her,

698
00:44:11,791 --> 00:44:14,053
then why can't he tell the truth?

699
00:44:14,053 --> 00:44:17,022
Why does it have to be a secret?

700
00:44:17,022 --> 00:44:20,039
"There's a secret message"?

701
00:44:20,039 --> 00:44:25,330
If I know, maybe he has a wife,
that's why he's keeping it a secret.

702
00:44:27,399 --> 00:44:30,943
We can't assume right away
the worst in people.

703
00:44:30,943 --> 00:44:34,440
Oh please, spare me.

704
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:36,241
Again, I disagree.

705
00:44:36,241 --> 00:44:39,978
Men can't be trusted.

706
00:44:39,978 --> 00:44:44,104
If their intentions were true,
why won't they show themselves?

707
00:44:44,104 --> 00:44:47,152
That's why as for me, swipe right away

708
00:44:47,152 --> 00:44:51,823
if the man has no picture
and no description in his profile.

709
00:44:53,559 --> 00:44:57,596
Don Ferell, it's you...

710
00:44:57,596 --> 00:44:59,431
I'm sorry, Don Ferell.

711
00:44:59,431 --> 00:45:04,136
Is there anything you need, Sir,
that's why you came to our nest?

712
00:45:04,136 --> 00:45:06,438
I just want to talk to Florence.

713
00:45:06,438 --> 00:45:09,088
We have something important to talk about.

714
00:45:10,142 --> 00:45:13,912
Okay, we'll leave you behind, Don Ferell.

715
00:45:13,912 --> 00:45:15,380
You better stay.

716
00:45:15,380 --> 00:45:17,582
You're included here. You're involved too.

717
00:45:18,517 --> 00:45:21,820
Did I do something bad?

718
00:45:21,820 --> 00:45:25,724
Sir, if Florence did something wrong,

719
00:45:25,724 --> 00:45:28,427
I will take full responsibility.

720
00:45:28,427 --> 00:45:30,496
After all, she's under me.

721
00:45:30,496 --> 00:45:34,099
And whatever mistake she did
is because of me,

722
00:45:34,099 --> 00:45:36,668
so I'll be the one to punish her.

723
00:45:37,770 --> 00:45:39,805
You didn't do anything wrong.

724
00:45:39,805 --> 00:45:42,818
I only have a request, actually.

725
00:45:42,818 --> 00:45:47,746
I want you to cook chopsuey for me.

726
00:45:47,746 --> 00:45:49,414
Huh?

727
00:45:49,414 --> 00:45:54,019
That's my favorite,
but ever since my wife died,

728
00:45:54,019 --> 00:45:57,622
I haven't tasted a delicious chopsuey.

729
00:45:58,557 --> 00:46:01,126
Of course, Don Ferell, we can do that.

730
00:46:01,126 --> 00:46:03,328
No problem.

731
00:46:03,328 --> 00:46:05,964
Actually, I don't want to contradict myself.

732
00:46:05,964 --> 00:46:12,192
Remember we agreed that Florence
will decide what to cook for this household.

733
00:46:12,192 --> 00:46:15,474
But please grant the request of an old man.

734
00:46:15,474 --> 00:46:20,979
I'm longing for the previous life
I had with my beloved wife.

735
00:46:20,979 --> 00:46:22,147
Is that all?

736
00:46:22,147 --> 00:46:25,184
No problem. It's just a small thing.

737
00:46:25,184 --> 00:46:26,485
Small thing?

738
00:46:26,485 --> 00:46:28,535
She means nothing to worry about.

739
00:46:28,535 --> 00:46:30,121
She can do it.

740
00:46:30,121 --> 00:46:32,024
This means to say,

741
00:46:32,024 --> 00:46:35,360
you'll be needing freshly picked vegetables,

742
00:46:35,360 --> 00:46:39,765
because that's how Dona Ferell used to do it.

743
00:46:39,765 --> 00:46:44,969
She gets the vegetables
from the Ferell's farms.

744
00:46:46,539 --> 00:46:49,041
You can go to the farm early morning,
tomorrow.

745
00:46:49,041 --> 00:46:53,714
From what I heard,
our produce is ready for harvest.

746
00:46:53,714 --> 00:46:57,249
I'll ask Nero to drive you.

747
00:46:57,249 --> 00:46:58,364
What?

748
00:46:58,364 --> 00:46:59,528
Nero?

749
00:46:59,528 --> 00:47:01,270
I'll ask Mr. Dencio.

750
00:47:01,270 --> 00:47:03,091
Dencio and I are going somewhere.

751
00:47:03,091 --> 00:47:04,557
How about Mr. James?

752
00:47:04,557 --> 00:47:08,105
Oh, I'm sorry, I'll be using James tomorrow

753
00:47:08,105 --> 00:47:12,575
because I have an important appointment
in the spa.

754
00:47:12,575 --> 00:47:15,601
I can commute.

755
00:47:15,601 --> 00:47:19,810
Don't give yourself a hard time.
I can ask Nero to bring you there.

756
00:47:19,810 --> 00:47:23,909
And he is known in that place,
he grew up there.

757
00:47:23,909 --> 00:47:28,313
My grandson is sulking, so let him go out
of his dugout once in a while

758
00:47:28,313 --> 00:47:31,116
and get some sunlight
so that he can have vitamin D.

759
00:47:31,116 --> 00:47:32,952
I agree.

760
00:47:32,952 --> 00:47:35,955
That's so correct, Don Ferell.

761
00:47:37,590 --> 00:47:39,358
Okay, no problem.

762
00:47:39,358 --> 00:47:42,027
I'll ask Nero to go with me tomorrow.

763
00:47:43,062 --> 00:47:52,843
<i>♪ Chopsuey... Chopsuey ♪</i>

764
00:47:52,843 --> 00:47:54,093
Florence, what's for breakfast?

765
00:47:54,093 --> 00:47:56,562
There, it's right in front of you,
ready to bite you.

766
00:47:56,562 --> 00:47:58,811
Happy Morning, Troy and Owen.

767
00:47:58,811 --> 00:48:00,813
- What do you want to eat?
- Wait a second.

768
00:48:00,813 --> 00:48:02,982
Why is there favoritism here?

769
00:48:04,250 --> 00:48:06,429
I thought you'll never visit us here.

770
00:48:06,429 --> 00:48:07,653
Is that possible?

771
00:48:07,653 --> 00:48:09,288
Who are you with?

772
00:48:09,288 --> 00:48:13,659
I'm Florence Dela Cruz.
I'm the cook in the mansion right now.

773
00:48:13,659 --> 00:48:15,897
Mother told me that often than not,

774
00:48:15,897 --> 00:48:20,366
the outside appearance is different
from what's inside.

775
00:48:20,366 --> 00:48:23,888
So if you want to know them better,

776
00:48:23,888 --> 00:48:25,471
you should knock on their hearts.

777
00:48:25,471 --> 00:48:27,140
Let me ask you.

778
00:48:27,140 --> 00:48:32,311
What if the person
whose heart you're knocking

779
00:48:32,311 --> 00:48:35,915
refuses to let you in his life?

780
00:48:35,915 --> 00:48:37,234
I will just keep on knocking...

781
00:48:37,234 --> 00:48:40,671
Knock, knock, knock until he opens the door.

782
00:48:40,671 --> 00:48:43,073
If I need to shout, I will shout.

783
00:48:43,073 --> 00:48:47,644
Hey, let me in your heart!
